1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
For twenty years, enterprise software ran on a simple business model:

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
build a web dashboard, charge a monthly tax for every employee who logs in,

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,800
and hope no one notices how little it is actually used.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,500
But according to a major forecast from research firm Gartner,

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,800
up to $234 billion in enterprise software spending is now at risk of disruption.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,500
Not because companies are using less software...

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:32,800
but because autonomous AI agents no longer need human dashboards to get work done.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,800
To understand why this is happening, look at how SaaS became one of the most profitable models on earth.
